      "message": "Strangely I got Android Canary build failures on another CL related to a use of GrMipMapped that I hadn\u0027t changed. Anyway, that prompted me to knock out the remaining internal  uses of the type alias.\n\nBTW, I notice we now have skgpu::graphite:Mipmapped (and Protected and maybe others). Should we be putting things like that in skgpu:: and sharing? I can\u0027t imagine them ever diverging and clients wouldn\u0027t have to type graphite:: every time they use it. We could always have using GrMipmapped \u003d skgpu::graphite so we don\u0027t need to rewrite all the existing clients.",
